e six Highlights pipeline verbs work unchanged [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]under `bob ref` and under the permanent `bob highlights` and `bob [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]highlights-ref` aliases. Annotations no longer carry the leaked [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]marker mirror, and a URL that only a legacy note records can be [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]captured again. A deployed `bob_ref` skill makes \"check the library[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]first\" the default step for agents that recommend reading.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]11[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]bob_ref_reference_library.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/bob_ref_reference_library.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-4w[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-4w/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Promote bob ref to the canonical command[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]rename[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rename: make `ref` the canonical Vault command with permanent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`highlights` and `highlights-ref` aliases, grouped help, canonical [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]diagnostics, completion paths, fixtures, docs, and alias-equivalence [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Managed-region and note-anatomy parser[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]region[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]region: a read-only parser for rendered ref-note bodies (annotation [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]blocks with quote and comment kept apart, tombstones, mirror and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]preamble detection, the user's own notes, and the Tasks section), [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]round-tripped against the renderer.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Read-only ref index, reading state, and identity[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]index[dim] · [dim][/dim]after region[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]index: a new `ref_library` module that builds one read-only row per ref [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]note (status precedence, derived reading state, identity keys, dates, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]origin, supersession, diagnostics, coverage) plus query resolution and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]title scoring, over a mixed-corpus fixture vault.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob ref find and the library CLI plumbing[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]find[dim] · [dim][/dim]after rename, index[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]find: add the Library help group, shared output plumbing and JSON [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]envelope, `docs/ref.md`, and batch identity lookup with verdicts, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]optional intake checks, and human, Markdown, and JSON output.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob ref list[/bold #D7AFFF]                                                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]list[dim] · [dim][/dim]after find[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]list: the reading queue by default and filtered library views (reading [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]state, status, type, origin, parent, since), with a consistent cap, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]opt-in Git dates, and grouped human output.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob ref show[/bold #D7AFFF]                                                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]show[dim] · [dim][/dim]after list[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]show: exact resolution of one or more references and their metadata, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]annotations (quote and comment kept apart), the user's own notes, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tasks, as human, Markdown digest, or JSON.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Library health and coverage rows in doctor[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]doctor[dim] · [dim][/dim]after rename, index[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]doctor: add warning-level library rows to `bob ref doctor`: index [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]totals, diagnostics, duplicate identities, leaked mirrors, and the count[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]of unindexed zorg-era reading records outside the ref directory.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Remove leaked marker mirrors and stamp completion dates[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]sync-fixes[dim] · [dim][/dim]after rename, region[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sync-fixes: fix bob-cli-4r so neither sidecar preambles nor marker [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mirrors render as annotations, drop previously leaked blocks without [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tombstones while keeping every genuine block ID stable, and stamp [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]completion or cancellation dates when sync closes a `^ref` task.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Capture URLs that only a legacy note records[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]legacy-capture[dim] · [dim][/dim]after rename[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]legacy-capture: shared dedupe refuses only PDF-backed note hits, 